  "name": "Cloister",
  "description": "A small sacred ensemble for a ruined mountain monastery, from Virtual Playing Orchestra and VSCO 2. A female choir sings the wordless line and a solo cello answers it, a concert harp turns the chords over, violins and violas hold the harmony, and cello and bass sections sit on the roots. A tubular bell tolls from far off and a celesta catches the light. Two parts wait for the intensity to rise: a male choir, and the hand drums and gong of the VCSL ritual kit. Everything is in one long hall, wetter than Hearthwild, so the room is part of the piece.",
